<section class="content-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Legal &amp; Compliance Framework</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Section 142(1)(i):</strong> Require filing of return (non-filers)</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 142(1)(ii):</strong> Require production of accounts and documents</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 142(1)(iii):</strong> Require information, notes, workings</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 142(2A):</strong> Special audit direction (with CIT approval)</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 271(1)(b):</strong> Penalty Rs 10,000 for non-compliance</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 276D:</strong> Prosecution &ndash; imprisonment up to 1 year + fine</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 144:</strong> Best Judgement Assessment (if no response)</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 143(2):</strong> Scrutiny notice (may follow 142(1))</li>
                    <li><strong>Faceless Assessment:</strong> NeAC &rarr; AU (ReAC) &rarr; VU &rarr; TU &rarr; RU</li>
                    <li><strong>Account Limit:</strong> AO can request accounts for last 3 years only</li>
                    <li><strong>Response:</strong> E-filing portal under E-Proceedings; typically 15 days</li>
                </ul>
                <p><strong>Filing Portal:</strong> <a href="https://www.incometax.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">incometax.gov.in</a> (e-filing portal)</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ SECTION -->
<section id="faq-section" class="content-section" style="background-color: #ffffff;">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <div class="faq-expanded">
                <aside class="faq-expanded__aside">
                    <h2 class="faq-expanded__title">Frequently Asked Questions &ndash; IT Notice Section 142(1) in Mumbai</h2>
                    <p class="faq-expanded__lead">Get answers about what 142(1) means, response time, non-compliance consequences, scrutiny vs inquiry, document scope, faceless assessment, partial compliance, and personal hearings.</p>
                    @include('partials.bigin-form', [
                        'variant'  => 'compact',
                        'service'  => 'IT Notice Section 142(1)',
                        'city'     => 'Mumbai',
                    ])
                </aside>
                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What does a Section 142(1) notice mean?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Inquiry notice before/during assessment requiring: file return (if not filed), produce accounts/documents, or furnish specific information. Not a demand or penalty &ndash; it's a request. But non-compliance: Rs 10,000 penalty, best judgement (S144), or prosecution (S276D). Patron analyses and responds for Mumbai taxpayers.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How much time to respond?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Time specified in notice &ndash; typically 15 days in faceless assessment. Extension possible through e-filing portal with valid reasons. Non-response triggers penalty and potential best judgement assessment. Patron submits well within deadline for Mumbai taxpayers.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What happens if I don't respond?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Three consequences: (1) Rs 10,000 penalty per failure (S271(1)(b)). (2) Best judgement assessment (S144) &ndash; AO estimates income from available info (always adverse). (3) Prosecution up to 1 year (S276D). Non-response damages compliance record. Patron ensures timely response.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is 142(1) the same as scrutiny?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>No. 142(1) is preliminary inquiry (information request). 143(2) is scrutiny (formal assessment). But 142(1) often precedes 143(2). Satisfactory 142(1) response may close case without scrutiny. Comprehensive response at this stage can prevent escalation for Mumbai taxpayers.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can AO ask for any document?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Almost, but with limits. Accounts only for last 3 years before previous year. Assets &amp; liabilities statement needs Joint Commissioner approval. Even if document seems irrelevant, compliance mandatory &ndash; relevance argument doesn't excuse non-production. Patron advises Mumbai taxpayers.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How does faceless assessment affect response?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Notice from NeAC, not local AO. Response on e-filing portal under E-Proceedings. Case assigned to AU in any ReAC. No face-to-face. Written response must be comprehensive and self-contained. Patron drafts detailed documented responses for Mumbai taxpayers.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What if I partially comply?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Better than non-compliance but can still attract penalty. Submit what you have with written explanation for unavailable items. Request additional time. Patron manages partial compliance demonstrating good faith for Mumbai taxpayers.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-8">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can I request personal hearing?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Even in faceless assessment, video conference hearing available through e-filing portal. Useful for complex cases. For exceptions to faceless (search cases, international tax): local AO hearing. Patron requests and represents at hearings for Mumbai taxpayers.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Quick Answers -->
            <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:32px;">
                <p><strong>Quick Answers</strong></p>
                <p><strong>Section 142(1) ka notice aaya hai &ndash; kya kare?</strong> E-filing portal pe jaao, E-Proceedings mein notice padho. Kya maanga hai: return file karo (142(1)(i)), documents do (142(1)(ii)), ya information likho (142(1)(iii)). 15 din mein respond karo. AIS data match karo ITR se. Patron 2 din mein analyse karke 10 din mein response file karta hai.</p>
                <p><strong>Respond nahi kiya toh kya hoga?</strong> Rs 10,000 penalty (Section 271(1)(b)). Section 144 mein AO khud income estimate karega &ndash; hamesha zyada hogi. Prosecution bhi ho sakta hai (1 saal jail). Patron ensure karta hai timely complete response.</p>
                <p><strong>Yeh scrutiny notice hai kya?</strong> Nahi. 142(1) preliminary inquiry hai &ndash; information maang raha hai. 143(2) scrutiny hai &ndash; full assessment. Lekin agar 142(1) ka response achha ho toh scrutiny tak jaane ki zarurat nahi. Patron aise response draft karta hai jo case close karwa de.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

